file: "packages/core/src/delta/diff_color.ts"
doc:
  "The one rule that maps a resolved colour and a change type to the colour a diff render paints.\n"
  "\n"
  "Vocabulary for this file is fixed in delta_overlay.spec.textproto."

methods: [
  { name: "diffColorFor"
    doc:
      "The colour a diff render should paint in place of `color`, given the\n"
      "change type of the element it belongs to.\n"
      "\n"
      "Two branches, tested in this order:\n"
      "\n"
      "1. UNCHANGED, or CHANGE_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED -> desaturate(color). This\n"
      "   runs whether `diffRoles` is defined or not, and never reads it.\n"
      "   Unchanged context is muted the same way in every theme.\n"
      "2. ADDED, MODIFIED or DELETED -> table mode when `diffRoles` is\n"
      "   defined, rotate mode when it is undefined.\n"
      "     table mode  -> diffRoles.added, diffRoles.modified or\n"
      "       diffRoles.deleted, the one matching the change type, returned\n"
      "       as-is. `color` is discarded; nothing is derived from it.\n"
      "     rotate mode -> rotateHue(color, d), where d is one of 90, 180 or\n"
      "       270 CHOSEN PER COLOUR, as below.\n"
      "\n"
      "ROTATE MODE, in full. Four states share the hue wheel -- unchanged is\n"
      "the base colour itself -- so the quadrants are the slots, and the\n"
      "three that are not the base go to the three change types.\n"
      "\n"
      "Which change type gets which quadrant is NOT fixed. It is derived from\n"
      "the base colour, in this order:\n"
      "  ADDED    takes whichever of +90/+180/+270 lands nearest hue 120\n"
      "           (green), measured as the shorter arc.\n"
      "  DELETED  takes whichever of the two REMAINING slots lands nearest\n"
      "           hue 0 (red).\n"
      "  MODIFIED takes the one slot left.\n"
      "A base with no hue -- not a six-digit hex, or fully desaturated --\n"
      "has no nearest anything: return rotateHue(color, 90), which is the\n"
      "identity on a grey, so such a colour comes back unchanged.\n"
      "\n"
      "Choosing per colour is what keeps the OUTPUT consistent. Rotation is\n"
      "relative, so one fixed angle cannot mean one colour: +270 reaches\n"
      "green from an azure base and cyan from a violet one. Picking the\n"
      "nearest quadrant per base makes ADDED read green and DELETED read red\n"
      "as closely as each base allows, which is the property a reader\n"
      "actually needs. The rotations differ between elements; the colours do\n"
      "not.\n"
      "\n"
      "Worked, against the bundled blueprint palette:\n"
      "  node   #8ad1ff -> added #96ff8a green, removed #ffb88a orange\n"
      "  edge   #73daca -> added #b7da73 chartreuse, removed #da7383 red\n"
      "  group  #bb9af7 -> added #d6f79a chartreuse, removed #f79aa8 red\n"
      "Quadrants are 90 apart, so a base sits at worst 45 from one; added is\n"
      "always nearer green than red and removed always nearer red than\n"
      "green, which is the invariant to test rather than any one hex.\n"
      "\n"
      "This function performs no validation on `color` and never inspects\n"
      "its format. A `color` that is not a hex string reaches rotateHue or\n"
      "desaturate, both of which return it unchanged; in table mode it is\n"
      "not read at all."
    inputs: [
      { name: "color",     type: { primitive: CHARACTER } },
      { name: "change",    type: { named: { symbol: "archeglyph.content.v1.ChangeType" } } },
      { name: "diffRoles", type: { named: { symbol: "DiffRoles" } }, is_optional: true }
    ]
    output: { primitive: CHARACTER }
    uses: ["rotateHue", "desaturate"]
  }
]
